# Fixed defect 131's class, 2026-09-29, one missing `]` in a type. Symptom:
# `n: [i64 @= [3]` cost the lexer's `unclosed_bracket` at the `[` and the
# parser's `expected_array_close` at the `@`: one missing closer, two
# messages. Cause: the lexer names every opener still open at the file's
# end, and the parser, reading the same brackets, named the closer it met
# missing too. Now the parser asks the tokens the lexer's own question, by
# the lexer's own stack, and where no closer closes the opener it names no
# closer and recovers past none, so the lexer's report is the one message
# (`selfhost/parse/unclosed.hero`). The lexer reads every line after an
# opener that never closes as inside it, so this case holds one, on its
# last line.

function main()
    print(1)

function g()
    n: [i64 @= [3]  #~ unclosed_bracket
